development.question_text:
Sketch $y=x^{3}-8$, showing the intercepts and the point of inflection.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3.2,0)--(3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.6)--(0,3.6) node[above] {$y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.solution_text:
1. **State the end behaviour as $x\to\infty$.**
As $x\to\infty$, $y\to\infty$ (positive cubic).
2. **Find the $y$-intercept by letting $x=0$.**
$y=0^{3}-8=-8$
3. **Find the $x$-intercept by letting $y=0$.**
$0=x^{3}-8$
$x^{3}=8$
$x=2$
4. **Mark the point of inflection $(b,c)$ and draw the curve.**
Point of inflection at $(0,-8)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3.2,0)--(3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.6)--(0,3.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1:2.5,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.35*(\x*\x*\x-8)});
\fill (2,0) circle (2pt);
\node[above right] at (2,0) {$(2,0)$};
\fill (0,-2.8) circle (2pt);
\node[left] at (0,-2.8) {$(0,-8)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

