mastery.solution_text:
1. **State the end behaviour as $x\to\infty$.**
As $x\to\infty$, $y\to-\infty$ (negative cubic).
2. **Find the $y$-intercept by letting $x=0$.**
$y=-2(0-3)^{3}+2=-2(-27)+2=56$
3. **Find the $x$-intercept by letting $y=0$.**
$0=-2(x-3)^{3}+2$
$2(x-3)^{3}=2$
$(x-3)^{3}=1$
$x=4$
4. **Mark the point of inflection $(b,c)$ and draw the curve.**
Point of inflection at $(3,2)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-1,0)--(6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3)--(0,9.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=0:5.1,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.15*(-2*(\x-3)*(\x-3)*(\x-3)+2)});
\fill (0,8.4) circle (2pt);
\node[right] at (0,8.4) {$(0,56)$};
\fill (3,0.3) circle (2pt);
\node[above right] at (3,0.3) {$(3,2)$};
\fill (4,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below] at (4,0) {$(4,0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
